      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/35a633/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2018-08-27T02:14:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I would think that immunity counts as prevented. A villian target targets stuntman for damage the damage is prevented as stuntman is immune to damage.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I do have a related question to moving target, it says \"When stuntman is dealt damage by a villain target, destroy this card and use a power.\" I was in a game with fixed point in time in play and when he took damage nothing happened. I wasn't sure if the card destruction was tied to the power use, but the game&nbsp;<span><span>interrupted </span></span>it that way.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:54:22.340Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
